  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Inflow arcs, beam arcs and sparks vary per cast. Orb growth and beam timing stay fixed for gameplay readability."
  },
  "director_notes": "The 130 ms overload beat is the key choice: a beat of instability right before release makes the payoff land harder. The beam itself has low jaggedness so it reads as a controlled beam, while the attached arcs add chaos on top. Decals: a spinning rune circle under the caster (add) sells the charge from every view, even edge-on; the beam end scorches a stretched mark (stretch along the cast direction, rotation 0) with a glowing burn while the beam is on."
